  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.7131 acc. Within the same family, avgpool+concat (0.6315) → avgpool+weighted (0.6776) shows a ~4.6pp gain from weighted fusion. However, we have not yet tested whether this fusion advantage persists when aggregation is switched to transformer. Question: config_032 (identical to config_033 except fusion=concat) isolates the single variable of fusion method under transformer aggregation. If concat ≈ weighted, then fusion choice is secondary to aggregation and we can simplify the design; if concat << weighted, it confirms weighted fusion is essential regardless of aggregation. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean one-variable comparison against the current best, has the highest expected performance among untested configs, and directly reduces uncertainty about whether the weighted-fusion gain seen with avgpool generalizes to transformer—information that determines which fusion strategy to lock in before exploring other axes (e.g., scgpt encoder or ViT-L image backbone)."
}

